WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.504
Step 1: Download the ZIP from the install page.

2
00:00:07.904 --> 00:00:11.904
Step 2: Unzip it into a folder you’ll keep. Chrome loads Link Meteor from there.

3
00:00:12.304 --> 00:00:15.008
Step 3: Open chrome://extensions and turn on Developer mode.

4
00:00:15.108 --> 00:00:18.303
Step 3: Then choose Load unpacked.

5
00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:22.503
Select the unzipped folder, the one that contains manifest.json.

6
00:00:22.903 --> 00:00:26.397
Link Meteor 1.0.0 now appears in your extensions.

7
00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:30.397
Step 4: Pin it from the puzzle-piece menu so the icon stays in view.

8
00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:34.063
Step 5: On the practice page, press the shortcut…

9
00:00:34.163 --> 00:00:37.683
Step 5: …and drag across one section.

10
00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:40.273
Compare the count with the section’s answer key: 9 links.

11
00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.240
Copy text + URL puts two columns on your clipboard.

12
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.799
Or add them to a collection to review later.

13
00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:49.926
Step 6: Click the Link Meteor icon to open its side panel beside the page.

14
00:00:50.026 --> 00:00:54.640
Step 6: Export shows exactly which links it will use.

15
00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.243
Step 6: Pick a format and download. Here, CSV.

16
00:00:57.643 --> 00:01:01.131
If the shortcut doesn’t work, change it at chrome://extensions/shortcuts.

17
00:01:01.531 --> 00:01:06.111
Help, bug reports and suggestions are under About and help.

18
00:01:06.211 --> 00:01:09.211
Reports are public, so leave out private URLs and data.
